ent-ClothingOuterWinterAtmos = atmospherics winter coat
    .desc = If you're cold, he's cold. Get Tropico out of the Atmospheric bay.
ent-ClothingOuterWinterCE = chief engineer's winter coat
    .desc = Was your hardsuit stolen again?
ent-ClothingOuterWinterChem = chemistry winter coat
    .desc = A fluffy insulated labcoat tucked beneath a tough acid-resistant apron. Kind of makes you look like a bartender. Maybe serve some drinks.
ent-ClothingOuterWinterCMO = chief medical officer's winter coat
    .desc = A large and expensive labcoat fitted with extra insulation for particularly cold operating rooms.
ent-ClothingOuterWinterEngi = engineering winter coat
    .desc = Atmos messed up and the air is at a cool 20 Kelvin? Better bundle up.
ent-ClothingOuterWinterGen = genetics winter coat
    .desc = An insulated labcoat meant to withstand the harsh chill of genome freezers.
ent-ClothingOuterWinterMed = medical winter coat
    .desc = A medical-grade labcoat fitted with extra insulation. Still quite handy against caustic spills, while staying comfortably warm.
ent-ClothingOuterWinterViro = virology winter coat
    .desc = A sterile, padded labcoat meant to protect from both types of cold.
